{"authored" [{"question" "q-317038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n  \n\n| $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider a general vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ -2x+7y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ -2x+7y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317038" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f4e7091e4ee56be98695f773fd266de658bdf2c1b27307304b6fc62f088bb32" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317038" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317038" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317038" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-317038" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2x+7y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $v$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $T,$ find $T(v).$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the fact that $\\,T(v)=T\\cdot v,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37881" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f4e7091e4ee56be98695f773fd266de658bdf2c1b27307304b6fc62f088bb32" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37881" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2y-5z+x \\\\ z-y+3x \\\\ -z-2x+3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $3\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4f4e7091e4ee56be98695f773fd266de658bdf2c1b27307304b6fc62f088bb32" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3bd742b55b514" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/state.json" "file_sha256" "ef79fac0f0455f96a11e5e8b513de98929eb5b97d1be5429adc3