veloper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5431.json" "file_sha256" "c606129d9da5ffb0b7d86efa8f5acf38ce7c71e5674f4d587ec68c2df22252dc" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n    Notice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5431.json" "file_sha256" "c606129d9da5ffb0b7d86efa8f5acf38ce7c71e5674f4d587ec68c2df22252dc" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ whose standard matrix is $[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5433.json" "file_sha256" "1d5f00300878dcf71bc5f594f5818b1b1c9dbd133a7d7357a8a277158e39b7be" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5433" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider a general vector $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ -5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8x-y \\\\ -5x-2y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,\\mathbf{T}\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5433.json" "file_sha256" "1d5f00300878dcf71bc5f594f5818b1b1c9dbd133a7d7357a8a277158e39b7be" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $T$ and the vector $\\mathbf{v}$ given below. If $T$ is the standard matrix of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ find $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}).$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5434.json" "file_sha256" "03e3178afb3a62c4db1ea033e7435ac03875fc1f8025732ed8e3ff5419d6018b" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5434" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the fact that $\\,\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})=T\\cdot \\mathbf{v},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =T\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 7 \\\\ -6 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}27 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5434.json" "file_sha256" "03e3178afb3a62c4db1ea033e7435ac03875fc1f8025732ed8e3ff5419d6018b" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5432.json" "file_sha256" "ec9136f469b3b707a2daa92bf1e5b5d2d5751583a26641e1672b94166cbf9399" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-5432" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNotice that\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n    \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/example-5432.json" "file_sha256" "ec9136f469b3b707a2daa92bf1e5b5d2d5751583a26641e1672b94166cbf9399" "basis" 854 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979728/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-168105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is \n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/state.json" "file_sha256" "16f2a424911c18198815e45fda4977066b130d2a6fe4b0ac57cd591b4f6b7b1f" "basis" 1112 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-168105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider a general vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y+z \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+z \\\\ -y+z \\\\ x-y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/state.json" "file_sha256" "16f2a424911c18198815e45fda4977066b130d2a6fe4b0ac57cd591b4f6b7b1f" "basis" 1112 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-168105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3d9df000b8d04304601ba1ed0194385592924551b158acc1ccd751b48fece3e" "basis" 1112 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-168105" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/state.json" "file_sha256" "16f2a424911c18198815e45fda4977066b130d2a6fe4b0ac57cd591b4f6b7b1f" "basis" 1112 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14005887/edb-import/verification.json"} {"qu