apture-workers/linear/14048912/state.json" "file_sha256" "5578abe544083bb020bc567f821bf5cccd4f5d4cd97fa48ccd6abe528b5372e8"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $T$, where\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}2y-5z+x \\\\ z-y+3x \\\\ -z-2x+3y\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/state.json" "file_sha256" "5578abe544083bb020bc567f821bf5cccd4f5d4cd97fa48ccd6abe528b5372e8"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe require a $3\\times 3$ matrix $T$ such that\n\n$$\nT\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x+2y-5z \\\\ 3x-y+z \\\\ -2x+3y-z\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $T$ is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/state.json" "file_sha256" "5578abe544083bb020bc567f821bf5cccd4f5d4cd97fa48ccd6abe528b5372e8"} {"question" "q-74944" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14048912/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6134ddf7b57f55c89c7bc4c99506f